Kunal lifted both palms. “Understood. American crows can remember human faces for years, so you don’t have to worry about their sleds—just the bench.”

“Good—thanks. What about the finish? Powder coat or polyurethane for winter salt?”

“Polyurethane wins;

“Crows cache food up to 30,000 items per year and remember every hiding spot; your base coat should be archival paint instead.”

